>
  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>Cabin crew work is a good career in India for people who enjoy service, shifts and travel and who plan what comes after, and a poor fit for those who expect a long steady climb in the same role.</strong> The decisions that unlock high income opportunities are building a second skill during the cabin years and a high-income skill portfolio that carries on after them.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Verdict:</strong> a real job with a short peak. Plan the next career from the first year.</li>
      <li><strong>Evidence:</strong> one airline lists Class 12 with 50 percent marks and an age of 18 to 27 for freshers. We found no dependable independent Indian pay data, and no academy can guarantee a seat.</li>
      <li><strong>Growth:</strong> training and standards roles, a side service and a degree for ground management have the most headroom, and they are the base of an earlier path to financial freedom.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p>
    This guide is part of our set of <a href="/blog/career-options/">career options for every stream and degree</a>. Compare it with <a href="/blog/career-options/is-aviation-a-good-career-in-india/">aviation as a career</a>, <a href="/blog/career-options/is-pilot-a-good-career-in-india/">pilot as a career</a> and <a href="/blog/career-options/is-hotel-management-a-good-career-in-india/">hotel management</a>.
  </p>

  <nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Article sections">
    <p class="jump-nav__label">Jump to section</p>
    <ul class="jump-nav__list">
      <li><a href="#verdict">The verdict</a></li>
