      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Ignoring the stated criteria</div>
        <p>Read each airline's notice before you spend on preparation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">03</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Having no plan after the cabin</div>
        <p>Build a second skill and savings from year one.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">04</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Skipping the contract details</div>
        <p>Read terms on notice, housing and return clearly before signing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">05</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Treating a certificate as proof</div>
        <p>An airline's selection is the proof.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    Read the careers pages of two or three airlines, record a self-introduction and ask a teacher for feedback. Then decide whether to apply directly or build a degree first.
  </p>
  <p>
    A specialist can look at your strengths, finances and goals with you. A sensible first step is <a href="/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/student-career-guidance/">student career guidance</a>. The aim is a high-income skill portfolio and an earlier path to financial freedom.
  </p>

  <p>
    For agency, guiding and own-tour routes, read <a href="/blog/career-options/travel-and-tourism-career-india/">travel and tourism careers</a>.
  </p>

